# Provenance is a SHA-256 of the source bytes, so git must never rewrite them.
# Checking out with autocrlf turned starter/pubmed/data.csv from LF into CRLF,
# which changed its hash and broke the reproducible-rebuild guarantee. Disable
# end-of-line conversion for the whole tree: no file here benefits from it, and
# a data-provenance tool cannot afford bytes that differ per machine.
* -text
